  "body": "Fork synced at v0.18.0.\n\n**What changed:** new guide page `site/content/guide/order-of-operations.md` (weight 7): sequencing principles with reasons, how CamCraft reorders (browser drag, `reorder_operation` MCP tool, one undo step, same-setup only), program order = browser order, rest roughing / drill laws reading earlier stock / carried stock between setups, order-dependent refusals, simulation as the check, and a worked 5-operation plate example before/after. Links `@/guide/setups.md`, `operations.md`, `refusals.md`, `posting.md`.\n\n**How checked:** every CamCraft claim read against main's source (`mcp/order_tools.rs`, `operation/drill_reach.rs`, `drill_prior.rs`, `tool_law.rs`, `generate.rs`, mill3d \"Rest roughing\"). `zola build` in `site/` succeeds, no broken internal links.\n\n**Not exercised:** the page was not rendered in a browser. The thread-mill-an-undrilled-hole refusal (#992 / PR #1045) is still open and NOT on main, so the page says such order checks are not part of this release and does not quote them. \"Drill/tap matched to a prior hole\" has no explicit refusal on main; only the drill flute-reach and tap-core refusals are described. The page is not yet linked from the operations page or the workflows page (workflows #1263 is unmerged).\n\n**Follow-ups once merged:** link from workflows (#1263), workholding (#1262), troubleshooting (#1244) and the operations page; add the thread-mill refusal text when #1045 lands.\n\nChangelog: none\n\nFixes #1280\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX\n",
